    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d146">

                <pb facs="0264" n="194" xml:id="pg194"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 351.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-09-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 17, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I enclose for your information an extract
                    from a despatch of the 9th of June last from the minister resident of the United
                    States in Japan, relative to the cordial relations existing between himself and
                    the ministers of England and France in that empire.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                    <p>(The extract above referred to will be found under the head of “ Japan,” in
                        this series.)</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
